## Address Task 1 review findings for the staged ontology Generate contract

Context: Follow-up to the entry above. A review of Task 1 flagged four gaps:
missing staged eval coverage for the "no rewrite after a rejected validation"
and "no one-shot default path" invariants, an inconsistent constraint-kind
name for the at-least-one-entity rule, sequential `draft_revision` values
across unrelated staged examples that implied a false shared session, and an
inconsistent annotation placement in the SPEC identity table. No runtime
source code was changed; the attached implementation plan
(`/Users/benoit.cayla/.cursor/plans/staged-ontology-generate_6fc7e158.plan.md`)
was not edited.

Changes:

1. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl and
   tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl
   Added two new `staged`-tagged examples: `staged-no-rewrite-after-
   validation-001` (a rejected Stage 3 axioms output must be reported as a
   retryable failure and never resubmitted as an in-request rewrite) and
   `staged-no-one-shot-default-001` (no entry point may silently perform
   one-shot generation as a default path). Renamed the inconsistent
   `min_remaining_entities` constraint kind to the canonical
   `min_included_entities` used elsewhere for the same at-least-one-entity
   invariant. Replaced the sequential `draft_revision` values across
   independent staged examples (2..9) with non-sequential, example-specific
   values so no example implies it continues another's draft session.
   Dataset now has 27 rows (10 parsed-corpus + 3 legacy + 14 staged), all
   unique ids, byte-identical mirrors, valid JSONL.
2. .planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md
   Moved the `stage_entry_points` `(staged, planned)` annotation from the
   identity table's Field column into the Value column, consistent with the
   `max_owl_eval_rounds` row's annotation style. Added a ninth proposed
   staged eval dimension, `stage_no_one_shot_default`, matching the new
   dataset coverage. Updated §7 to describe 14 staged cases (was 12) and the
   two new required-coverage topics, and documented the runner's new
   required-constraint-kind check. Updated the §10 sign-off note to record
   the 14-example validation result.
3. tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py
   Raised `_MIN_STAGED_EXAMPLES` from 10 to 14 to match the current staged
   row count, and added `_REQUIRED_STAGED_CONSTRAINT_KINDS` — a coverage
   check asserting `stage_no_rewrite_after_reject` and
   `stage_no_one_shot_default` are each exercised by at least one staged
   example — so neither review-flagged gap can silently regress out of the
   dataset even if the row count is later satisfied by unrelated additions.
   Verified the new checks actually fail by temporarily corrupting/removing
   staged rows, then restored the files and re-validated byte-identical
   mirrors.
4. .superpowers/sdd/progress.md (ignored; not committed)
   Added a "Three-stage ontology generate implementation" section
   referencing the plan file and recording the Task 1 and Task 1 fixes
   commits/baseline/test results.

